 ## Overview
-CPU Sparse Voxel Octree Traversal is a real-time ray traversal algorithm for sparse voxel octrees that uses a stack-based approach to navigate from the root to leaf voxels, calculating intersections with node boundaries to determine the next octant [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering large sparse voxel datasets on the CPU by avoiding the overhead of recursive function calls and leveraging explicit state management for cache-friendly memory access [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from [Recursive Octree Traversal](2632-recursive-octree-traversal.md) by using an explicit stack instead of the call stack, and from [Parametric Octree Traversal](2361-parametric-octree-traversal.md) by relying on discrete slab boundaries or DDA steps rather than parametric intervals for child selection [S2, unofficial].
